// Game: Postretro
// Format: Valve
// glossy-reflections-test dev map. A sealed main room, interior x 0 to 512,
// y 0 to 512, z 0 to 256, walls 32 thick. The floor is metal_smoothness_ramp
// at scale 8, a glossy floor; the north wall is concrete_carved_tinted_gloss
// at scale 8, a glossy wall; the ceiling's underside is concrete_carved_gloss
// at scale 8, a glossy down-facing ceiling; a 45 degree ramp against the west
// wall has a glass_gloss_tiles slope. The other walls and the pillar are
// concrete_stone_021, which has an _s map and no _p, so it never reflects.
// A full-height pillar stands on the floor in the north-east; a small
// freestanding monument of three brushes, plinth, column and cap, stands on
// the floor at the room centre; an animated light_area panel lies on the floor
// in the south-west, under the glossy ceiling. Two static point lights.
// Player start in the south-west corner facing the monument.
// A 32 unit doorway in the south wall at x 384 to 416, in line with the
// pillar, opens on a side wing south of the room: a hall at y -96 to -32
// and four 256 unit square rooms at y -384 to -128, z 0 to 256, that
// art-direct reflection through _p and _s alone. West of the doorway a
// fade-band room at x -608 to -352 and a floor-only room at x -320 to -64;
// east of it a highlights-only room at x 576 to 832 and a tile-and-grout
// room at x 864 to 1120. Each has a static point light, a ceiling
// light_area panel and a dim light_area glow band across the foot of its
// south wall. The only wing planes crossing the span of the room are the
// pillar planes x 384 and 416, so the room keeps its probes.
// Glossy placement runs only under prl-build --glossy-reflections.
// See glossy-reflections-test.README.md.
// NOTE: keep map comments free of braces and quotes, and never leave a blank
// line inside an entity block.
